# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# A key is OPTIONAL for development. Without one the app runs degraded:
# list view, place detail, itineraries and haversine distances all work.
# Only map rendering, Places search and Directions show placeholders.
# Build and review that path first — it is how CI and key-less preview
# deploys will see the app.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  WARNING: VITE_ variables are compiled into the client bundle.
#  Anyone can read them in devtools. There is no way to hide a key in a
#  frontend-only app.
#
#  The key is protected by HTTP referrer restrictions and quota caps in
#  Google Cloud — NOT by keeping this file secret. Configure those before
#  your first production deploy. See docs/07-Google-Maps.md.
#
#  Never put a secret that must stay secret in a VITE_ variable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Google Maps API key.
#
# Enable exactly these three APIs on it, and nothing else:
#   - Maps JavaScript API
#   - Places API
#   - Directions API
#
# Then restrict it:
#   1. Application restrictions → HTTP referrers:
#        http://localhost:5173/*
#        https://your-project.vercel.app/*
#        https://*-your-team.vercel.app/*        (preview deploys)
#        https://yourdomain.com/*
#   2. API restrictions → the three APIs above only
#   3. Set a DAILY QUOTA CAP on each one. Without a cap, a render loop or a
#      scraped key becomes a four-figure bill.
#   4. Set a billing budget alert.
#
# Use a SEPARATE key for local development and preview deploys, restricted
# to localhost and *.vercel.app. Keep the production key to your domain only.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Google Maps Map ID — must be a VECTOR map.
#
# Cloud Console → Maps → Map Management → Create Map ID → Vector.
# Required for AdvancedMarkerElement (our custom category-coloured pins) and
# for cloud-based map styling.
#
# Create two: one styled for light mode, one for dark. The dark style must be
# genuinely dark and warm to match the palette in docs/04-Design-System.md —
# Google's default "night" preset is blue and clashes badly.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
